    <string name="setup_progress">Setup progress</string>
    <string name="setup_start">Get started</string>
    <string name="setup_next">Next</string>
    <string name="setup_finish">Finish</string>
    <string name="setup_granted">Granted ✓</string>
    <string name="setup_fallback">Fallback</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_pitch">The edges of your screen light up whenever an app posts a notification.</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_privacy">Rimlit works offline: it has no network permission, so nothing it sees leaves your phone.</string>
    <string name="setup_access_title">Notice notifications</string>
    <string name="setup_access_desc">Rimlit needs notification access to notice when an app posts a notification, and to take a glow\'s colours from it. This step can\'t be skipped: without it Rimlit can\'t glow.</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_title">How to allow restricted settings</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_desc">Greyed out, or \"Restricted setting\"? Android blocks this for apps installed from outside an app store. Tap here to open Rimlit\'s App info, choose \"Allow restricted settings\" from its ⋮ menu, then try again.</string>
    <string name="setup_on_screen_title">Glow while the screen is on</string>
    <string name="setup_on_screen_desc">Rimlit draws over other apps in one of two ways. The accessibility glow is recommended: it also glows above the lock screen, without Android\'s \"displaying over other apps\" notification, and it only draws: it can\'t read or control anything on your screen. Display over other apps is the fallback.</string>
    <string name="setup_screen_off_title">Glow with the screen off</string>
    <string name="setup_screen_off_desc">To glow while the screen is off, Rimlit posts a silent notification that wakes the screen into a black, always-on-display style glow. Allow notifications, then full-screen notifications.</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_title">Glow on time</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_desc">Battery optimisation can hold Rimlit back, so a glow arrives late. Letting it run unrestricted keeps glows on time.</string>
    <string name="setup_fit_title">Fit your screen</string>
    <string name="setup_fit_desc">The glow follows your screen\'s corners and its camera cutout. The outline round this screen shows where it runs: adjust it if it doesn\'t sit right.</string>
    <string name="setup_pill_title">The app pill</string>
    <string name="setup_pill_desc">On-screen glows show which app is notifying in a small pill at the top. Move it if it doesn\'t sit right: drag a slider to see where it goes.</string>
    <string name="setup_look_title">Pick a first look</string>
    <string name="setup_look_desc">Every notification glows with your default look. Pick a style to start from; you can change it, and make more looks, at any time.</string>
    <string name="setup_look_keep">Keep \"%1$s\"</string>
    <string name="setup_look_customise">Customise it when setup is done</string>
    <string name="setup_test_title">Try it</string>
    <string name="setup_test_desc">Send yourself a test notification to see the glow, then finish to turn edge lighting on.</string>
    <string name="setup_test_preview">Preview the glow</string>
    <string name="setup_test_preview_note">Without notifications allowed, or with Rimlit\'s test notifications turned off, this shows a preview instead of a real test notification.</string>
    <string name="setup_test_window_note">Without a way to glow over other apps, this plays the glow here in Rimlit only. Real notifications won\'t glow until you allow one.</string>

